<title>FRANCE: French industrial production falls in January.</title>
<headline>French industrial production falls in January.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE said on Friday industrial production, excluding construction, fell 1.2 percent in January from the previous month but was up 1.6 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Industrial production excluding energy, agri-food businesses and construction -- considered by INSEE the best measure of manufacturing output -- was down 1.0 percent in January from the previous month, giving a year-on-year rise of 1.1 percent.</p>
<p>It gave the following seasonally adjusted data based on a new index introduced in January 1996.</p>
<p>The previous index used a base year of 1985.  </p>
<p>						    Jan 97 Dec 96  Nov 96</p>
<p>Industrial production index (base 1990)* 99.2  100.4   99.6</p>
<p>Manufacturing output*			  95.0   96.0   95.1</p>
<p>  Agri-food				     108.5  111.9  112.0</p>
<p>  Energy					  119.2  119.1  118.9</p>
<p>  Semi-finished goods			  99.5  100.3   99.9</p>
<p>  Industrial capital goods		   85.4   85.9   85.4</p>
<p>  Car Industry				  100.7  101.3  101.6</p>
<p>  Consumer goods				 95.6   98.1   94.2</p>
<p>  Construction				   79.8   88.7   86.2</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following seasonally adjusted percentage changes:</p>
<p>					Jan vs Dec  Dec vs Nov   yr/yr*</p>
<p> Industrial production index     -1.2	  0.8	   1.6</p>
<p> Manufacturing output		-1.0	  0.9	   1.1</p>
<p> Agri-food			     -3.0	 -0.1	   1.7</p>
<p> Consumer goods			-2.5	  4.1	  -1.2</p>
<p> Car industry			  -0.6	 -0.3	  -1.8</p>
<p> Industrial capital goods	  -0.6	  0.6	   0.6</p>
<p> Semi-finished goods		 -0.8	  0.4	   2.8</p>
<p> Energy				   0.1	  0.2	   4.5</p>
<p> Construction			 -10.0	  2.9	  -7.3</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom + 33 1 42 21 53 81</p>
